# Tcache Double-Free Exploit

## Vulnerability Overview

The tcache (thread-local caching) mechanism in glibc's malloc is vulnerable to double-free attacks because, prior to glibc 2.29, it had **no double-free detection whatsoever**. Even after the `key` field check was added in 2.29, the check can be bypassed by corrupting the key or using intermediate frees.

## Target Setup

```c
// vulnerable.c - compile with: gcc -o vulnerable vulnerable.c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>

int main() {
    setvbuf(stdout, NULL, _IONBF, 0);

    int choice;
    char buf[8];

    while (1) {
        printf("1. Allocate\n2. Free\n3. Write\n4. Exit\n> ");
        fgets(buf, sizeof(buf), stdin);
        choice = atoi(buf);

        if (choice == 1) {
            printf("Index: ");
            fgets(buf, sizeof(buf), stdin);
            int idx = atoi(buf);
            if (idx < 0 || idx >= 10) continue;
            if (chunks[idx]) continue;  // BUG: doesn't check if already allocated
            chunks[idx] = malloc(0x88);
            printf("Data: ");
            fgets(chunks[idx], 0x88, stdin);
        }
        // ... free allows freeing same index twice (no NULL-ing in some paths)
    }
}
```

